w23-world-consistent-history
----------------------------

This directory is a clean-room Python 3 standard-library method sketch. It is
original work for this repository and contains no third-party code, data,
traces, prompts, worlds, labels or weights.

Paper (method idea credited)
----------------------------
Egor Pakhomov, Anurag Koul, Hongjun Liu, Bo Pang, Shafiq Joty, Erik Nijkamp.
"Cleaning an Agent's History Hurts When the World Still Holds the Error".
arXiv:2611.14654, v1, submitted 10 Nov 2026 (v1 Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:06:36
UTC). Primary category cs.AI, cross-listed cs.CL and cs.LG.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.14654
Paper licence: CC BY 4.0, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
(shown on the abs page). Only the abstract is quoted or used.

Ancillary files
---------------
The arXiv comments field says "code and data in ancillary files". They were
not downloaded, not opened and not run. No code, data, trace, world, label
or output from them is used. They are UNVERIFIED here.

Method only: the idea that a history edit (compaction, repair or handoff)
must be judged against the world it describes, the two natural edits named
in the abstract (a truthful note beside the preserved error, and the
agent's own completed action), and the receipt-versus-effect contrast
(a success receipt while the effect is absent or present). The world-check
rule, the honest baseline, the receiver stub, its decision table, the
recovery score, the oracle and the fixtures are this sketch's own; no
receiver model is run. The paper's "database write" setting is borrowed
only as a generic world-effect value: this is not a database port. No text,
figures, tables or data from the paper are copied into the code; the PDF
was not read; no model was run. The paper's claims appear only in
paper_evidence.json, quoted and marked UNVERIFIED.
